            "showLineNumbers": false,
            "showMiniMap": false
          },
          "content": "### 📖 IRQ Observability \u0026 Category Reference Primer\n\n| Category | Devices \u0026 Subsystems Included | Purpose \u0026 Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Network** | `eth*`, `ena*`, `vfio*` | High-throughput NIC Rx/Tx queue interrupts. Primary source of network traffic latency. |\n| **Storage** | `nvme*`, `sd*`, `ahci*` | NVMe controller and disk I/O queues. |\n| **Accelerator** | `qat*` (Intel QAT), `idxd*` (Intel DSA), `fpga*` | Hardware offload engines for crypto, compression, and direct memory streaming. |\n| **System** | `timer`, `rtc`, `acpi`, `IOMMU`, `dmar`, `pciehp`, `PME`, `IO-APIC`, `ttyS*`, `smbus` | Platform clocks, VT-d DMA remapping, power management, and PCIe bus maintenance. |\n| **Other** | Unmapped hardware interrupts | Uncategorized kernel interrupts. |\n\n---\n\n* **Reporting Modes (`$report_type`)**: \n  * `active_1s`: Real-time 1-second active telemetry (`rate \u003e 0`) for DevOps microburst detection.\n  * `full_1m`: 1-minute complete compliance snapshot (includes idle `0`-rate IRQs) for trading team isolation verification.\n* **Metric Headers**: `rate` represents **IRQs/second**; `cumulative_count` represents total accumulated interrupts **since server boot**.",
          "mode": "markdown"
